// case: generic-union-empty-construction-needs-a-written-type
// what: `Option.Some(21)` decides the instantiation from the value it hands
//      to the payload. `Option.Some()` is a construction against the template
//      with an empty argument list, so the construction decides nothing and
//      no position writes a type: `val x` has no annotation. The read site
//      of `n118` stays silent here, because `Some` declares a payload and
//      the guard `unionVariantCarriesNoPayload` at
//      `compiler/front/sema.orb:4663` answers false. The refusal therefore
//      comes from the construction site `unionInstanceForConstruction` at
//      `compiler/front/sema.orb:688`, and it prints "nothing in the
//      construction" where `n118` measured "nothing in this expression".
// expect-error: carries no payload, so nothing in the construction says which instantiation
union Option[T] {
    Some(T)
    None
}

fn main() -> int {
    val x = Option.Some()
    return 0
}
